<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 23rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/23rd-century-bce">23rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manium was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magan">Magan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> land of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, known only from inscriptions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkad">Akkad</a>, who reigned in the 23rd century BCE. Naram-Sin claimed to have defeated him, quarried diorite in his mountains and carried it back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> to make statues. He is one of the earliest named rulers of eastern Arabia.</p></div>
